\par The Eden Repair Vehicle rolled at best possible speed toward the smoking Structure Factory, its limited intelligence plotting a course across irregular ground.  Then a new command came in from the Robot 
Command Center.  The vehicle slowed, turned about, and headed back toward the RCC itself.
\par 
\par It took only a few minutes to reach the structure, which was well away from the fighting and showed no sign of damage.  Nonetheless, the unit's new programming had to be obeyed.  It deployed its robot manipulator arms and cutting torches, and began to sli
ce away sections of the building's skin, peeling it like an onion and throwing the removed pieces aside without caution.
\par 
\par Gas exploded into the thin atmosphere as the
 pressure hull ruptured, but the unit ignored it, mindlessly widening the breach.  The program drove it relentlessly on.  Something had to be removed from the RCC, and the Repair Vehicle would not stop until it had done so.
\par 
\par }\pard \s15\qc\li360\ri360\widctlpar {\f5\cf4 # # #
\par }\pard \s15\li360\ri360\widctlpar {\f5\cf4 
\par Jix ran down the ramp from the Nursery's upper level.  "There are Eden tanks coming in.  The rescue convoy is pulling back."
\par 
\par "Frag it!" Brook watched as the teacher robots scooped up the last of the rescue balls and headed out.
\par 
\par "With the tunnel blocked," observed Oltion, "we can only go out, toward the Agridomes.  Maybe we can get the kids out that way."
\par 
\par Brook nodded.  "It's worth a shot.  But I don't know how the rescue convoy is going to find us all the way over there." He shrugged.  "We'll worry about that later." He and Jix followed the robots out through the lock.  They jumped into the seats of the c
argo cart, while the others grabbed scooters.
\par 
\par }\pard \s15\qc\li360\ri360\widctlpar {\f5\cf4 # # #
\par }\pard \s15\li360\ri360\widctlpar {\f5\cf4 
\par Emma followed Jensen down the dark, narrow utility tunnel.  "If I remember this properly," he said, "this will take us around the blockage and come out somewhere along Agridome row.  We can backtrack to the Nursery from there."
\par 
\par "If we need to," said Emma.
\par 
\par "What do you mean?"
\par 
\par "They'll be looking for another way out.  If I were them, I'd head for the Agridomes."
\par 
\par Jensen nodded.  "You could be right."
\par 
\par They reached a junction with another, slightly wider utility tunnel.  Jensen stopped and looked in both directions.  "I don't remember this."
\par 
\par Emma frowned at him.  "Are you }{\i\f5\cf4 sure}{\f5\cf4  you know where you're going?"
\par 
\par }\pard \s15\qc\li360\ri360\widctlpar {\f5\cf4 # # #
\par }\pard \s15\li360\ri360\widctlpar {\f5\cf4 
\par There were five Agridomes in the row.  Jix stopped at the second one.  "This is where I work.  I have all the access keys.  We may need them before we're through." They cycled the cart in through a big cargo lock and drove directly into the dome.
\par 
\par Greenery was everywhere, the crops in full production.  Planter boxes full of soil alternated with rows of long hydroponic trays under the transparent ceilings, and water pumped from a large, open cistern in the middle of the 
dome and into irrigation pipes and sprinklers.
\par 
\par An emergency pressure release pipe ran from a valve over the tank and straight up through the roof.  Brook studied the pipe.  "I think I know a way to signal the convoy.  Think you can find some hose or flexible conduit that will fit over that valve?

\par 
\par Jix nodded.
\par 
\par "Then get it."
\par 
\par Jix disappeared and returned a few minutes later with a piece of flexible ductwork just large enough to fit over the valve.
\par 
\par Brook inspected the end of it, and attempted to crush it b
etween his palms.  He was unable to do so.  "I hope this will work." He jammed one end over the valve and sealed it with a roll of tape that Jix found in the cart's toolbox.  Then he dropped the other end in the cistern.  He turned back to Jix.  "Find a c
ontrol panel and use your override codes to open this valve."
\par 
\par Jix followed the pipe up through the ceiling with his eyes, then looked sadly around at the plants.  "I hate this, you know." But he did as Brook instructed.  There was a panel on a support pill
ar a few meters away.  Jix punched in his codes.  "Ready," he said.
\par 
\par Brook nodded, and Jix opened the valve.
\par 
\par For a moment, nothing happened, then the water level in the cistern began to drop.  The vent pipe moaned and rumbled as the inside air pressure forced the liquid up through the ceiling.  The top of the pipe suddenly turned into a fountain, water streaming
 down the outside of the windows.  The Agridome was spouting like a whale.
\par 
\par Just then something clanked beneath their feet.
\par 
\par Jix jumped at the sound.  "Somebody's coming!"
\par 
\par A floor access panel flipped open suddenly and clanged against its stops.  An armored, gun-toting figure climbed out of the opening, followed quickly by another.  They strode toward Brook rapidly.  The one in the lead thrust out a hand at him.
\par 
\par Emma smiled at him through the visor of her combat suit.  "Mr.  Panati, I presume."
\par 
\par }\pard \s15\qc\li360\ri360\widctlpar {\f5\cf4 # # #
\par }\pard \s15\li360\ri360\widctlpar {\f5\cf4 
\par As the convoy made its way back past the collapsed tunnel, their precious cargo safely in the remaining ET, they could see the RLV climbing into the sky on a tail of fire.  "I hope it's under our control," said Emma.
\par 
\par Jensen was looking in another direction.  "Incoming Eden unit."
\par 
\par "Frag," said Emma as she followed his gaze to the approaching robot.  Fortunately, it was only a Repair Vehicle.  One of the EMP units fired, and it rolled to a stop.
\par 
\par Emma leaned forward, not believing her eyes.  A Savant computer was clutched in one of its manipulator arms.  "Get a Spider over here, fast.  Let's capture this thing."
\par 
\par She studied the featureless cube of the Savant, and was somehow sure it was Kraft.  }{\i\f5\cf4 It escaped.  Kraft programmed the Repair Vehicle to come and get it, and it escaped.}{\f5\cf4 
\par 
\par She turned to Jensen.  "When the Repair Vehicle comes back online, plot an indirect course into its computer, taking it to the resistance base.  We'll send Axen a little present."  }{\i\f5\cf4 
And we'll see just what he thinks about his computer's behavior now.
